            <ArticleTitle>Regioselective switching approach for the synthesis of α and δ carboline derivatives.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1676-1679</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c6cc09468f</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A metal-free protocol for accessing both α and δ-carboline derivatives, starting from a common indolylchalcone oxime ester precursor is reported. The reaction involves mild conditions and uses a regiodivergent approach. DDQ is used as a switching agent in selectively generating α and δ-carboline derivatives in good to moderate yields.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
